  "_note": [
    "THE SOURCE, AND A TEMPLATE. English (UK) is what this mod is written in, so this file is never read -- it is here to be COPIED. Rename the copy to your language's code, fill in the right-hand side, and put it back in this folder.",
    "",
    "The left-hand side is the English exactly as the mod says it. It has to match to the character, including the two spaces some prompts have before a price.",
    "",
    "Leave anything you do not want to translate empty, or delete the line. Either way it shows in English, which is the point: a half-finished file is a working mod in two languages, not a broken one.",
    "",
    "~INPUT_CONTEXT~ is the button the player has actually bound and the game draws it as a picture -- keep it, and put it where your sentence wants it. Same with {0} and {1}, which are a shop's name and a price. ~b~ ~c~ ~r~ ~s~ are colours; ~s~ turns the colour off again.",
    "",
    "Codes: en-GB en-US pt-BR es fr de ru pl zh hi."
